A||N||2||terryk||88 Front Engine Mount Bracket on a pre-88 Cradle?||||1||
Z||000000||terryk||06-16-2000||12:47 PM||||Does anyone know if the 88 front engine mount (u-bracket style) will work in place of the pre-88 L-bracket? This is the bracket the bolts to the motor and then to the front engine mount (not the trans).<P>I'm swapping a 3.4L DOHC into an 86 SE and while I can use the 86 front mount (and grind part of it down), the 88 mount will fit the block without mods. <P>What I don't know is if the holes for the mount will be located where the 86 mount is positioned?<P>Confused? Me too....<P>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Will||06-16-2000||01:15 PM||||For '88 the engine mount was moved forward about an inch to compensate for the '88 cradle not having the shock absorber that the early ones did.<BR>I have not seen an '88 V6 mount, though I would guess it would be pretty easy to drill an extra set of holes offset an inch aft of the original holes.<BR>I am doing a Northstar swap myself, but I would be very interested to hear how your project comes out.||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||06-16-2000||01:21 PM||||Hi Will,<P>Thanks for the reply. You're right. I phoned a friend that swapped the 88 cradle into his 85 and he said the L-bracket positioned the mount in the wrong location (and as you said, close, but off a bit.)<P>I'll use the L-bracket on the 86. One down, a million to go. I'll keep you posted.<P>Where are you on the NS swap? What are you doing for the axles?<P>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
